What is an S3 Presigned URL and why use it?


😊💞An S3 Pre-signed URL is a temporary URL generated by AWS that allows secure access to an S3 object for a limited time. It’s commonly used to let external users upload or download files without needing AWS credentials, while ensuring access automatically expires after the defined duration

✔️✔️Imagine you have a locked locker (S3 object). Normally, only people with the main key (IAM credentials) can open it.
A presigned URL is like giving someone a temporary key that works for, say, 10 minutes → after that, the key becomes useless.


🤞🤞Presigned URL = Temporary Access Ticket to S3 🎟️


1. Sharing Files

👉 Scenario: You have a private bucket with invoices. Your client needs to download their invoice, but you don’t want to make the bucket public.
	•	Question: How will you give them secure access?
	•	Answer: Generate a pre-signed URL valid for a short time (say 15 minutes) and share it. After expiry, the link won’t work.

⸻

2. Direct Uploads

👉 Scenario: A mobile app allows users to upload profile pictures. You don’t want your app servers to handle large files.
	•	Question: How will you let users upload securely?
	•	Answer: Generate a pre-signed URL with PUT permissions → app directly uploads to S3, no credentials exposed.

⸻

3. Temporary Team Access

👉 Scenario: A team member (not in AWS account) needs to download a dataset from S3 but only once.
	•	Question: How will you allow this without creating IAM users?
	•	Answer: Provide a pre-signed URL valid for a very short duration.

⸻

4. Expired Link Issue

👉 Scenario: You gave a client a pre-signed URL valid for 5 minutes, but they tried after 15 minutes.
	•	Question: What happens? How will you fix it?
	•	Answer: The link expires → they get AccessDenied. You need to generate a new pre-signed URL.

⸻

5. Security Concern

👉 Scenario: A pre-signed URL link leaked in a chat group.
	•	Question: Can everyone use it?
	•	Answer: Yes, anyone with the link can use it until expiry → so always keep expiry short and restrict access with bucket policies or signed cookies (if using CloudFront).

Pre-signed URL → Key with expiry (like a movie ticket 🎟️).
	•	Public Bucket → Always open (like a free park 🏞️).
	•	CloudFront Signed URL → Premium pass (like Netflix login 🎬).
